 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 515612,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "You’re planning a road trip with some friends. Though you have 6 friends you’d consider bringing along, you only have room for 3 other people in the car. How many different possibilities are there for your road trip squad?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>This is a combination. It doesn’t matter which order you choose the 3 friends out of 6 friends.</p>\n<p>The number of combinations of <i>n</i> objects taken <i>r</i> at a time is <span data-math=\"nCr = \\frac{{n!}}{{r!\\left( {n - r} \\right)!}}\"></span>.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"6C3 = \\frac{{n!}}{{r!\\left( {n - r} \\right)!}} = \\frac{{6!}}{{3!\\left( {6 - 3} \\right)!}} = \\frac{{6!}}{{3!3!}} = \\frac{{6 \\times 5 \\times 4 \\times \\cancel{{3!}}}}{{3 \\times 2 \\times 1 \\times \\cancel{{3!}}}} = \\frac{{120}}{6} = 20\"></span></p>\n<p>There are 20 ways to pick three other people.</p>\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "20"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
